1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Qupon — corporate actions engine for tokenized bonds on Solana.
Coupon, vote, redeem — fully on-chain.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:30,000
We create the bond as a Token-2022 mint, frozen by default.
Three investors pass the KYC gate — KYC itself is simulated —
an unregistered wallet is rejected on-chain.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Coupon one. The registrar announces it; at record date
the program pauses the mint and freezes the register.

4
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Snapshot writes an Entitlement per holder — half-up rounding
per holder: 500, 1,250, 3,250 tenge.
The issuer pre-funds escrow; the program checks the amount.

5
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Payment settles from escrow, the action PDA signs.
We reconcile, resume the register, and generate
ISO 20022 seev.036 confirmations and the KASE notice.

6
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:55,000
A bondholder meeting. Votes are weighted by snapshot units:
65 for, 25 against, 10 abstain.
Quorum 100 percent, approval over two-thirds — approved.

7
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The new rate lands in the series and the token metadata.
The next coupon pays 600, 1,500, 3,900.

8
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:35,000
At maturity: principal plus final coupon per holder,
then units are burned through the permanent delegate
and the mint closes. Status: redeemed.

9
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Bonus: an early call in USDC on a real KASE bond's terms,
with accrued-days interest, rounded half-up.

10
00:02:50,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Everything you saw is on Solana devnet. KYC, Swift delivery
and ARDFM registration are simulated and labelled.
Code and every transaction link are in the repo.
